  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Care for Wildlife at the Virginia Living Museum</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Virginia Living Museum is a leader in LIVING exhibits. It provides a home for 1,000 native animals representing 180 species of mammals, birds, reptiles, amphibians, and fish, including threatened and endangered species. Many animals have been rehabilitated and deemed un-releasable by veterinary professionals. Fully accredited, the Museum provides the animals a safe environment and enriching, natural habitats while they serve as ambassadors of their species - delighting &amp; educating guests.</narrative>
  </description>
